  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You call forth a fiendish spirit. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the Fiendish Spirit stat block. When you cast the spell, choose Demon, Devil, or Yugoloth. The creature looks like a Fiend of that kind, which determines some details of its stat block. It disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.</p><p>The creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count but takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you); if you give none, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-tmVbKqmiaaNur2eW\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Summon asks for the kind. The spirit’s AC, Hit Points, attack damage and Death Throes damage include the spell’s level, and Death Throes uses your spell save DC.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
